# Vercel serves /api/* and nothing else - its root is a 404, and the dashboard
# is hosted by GitHub Pages. Keeping the journal out is the point: it is
# committed every ten minutes during a session and is never read from the
# bundle, because api/journal.py fetches it live from the GitHub contents API.
#
# DELIBERATELY MINIMAL. An earlier version of this file also excluded
# pyproject.toml, agent/ and dashboard/, and every Vercel build from that
# commit onward failed - nine code pushes in a row never deployed, while the
# site kept serving a proxy that reported a $202,287 account. A failed build
# leaves the previous deployment running, so the breakage is silent. The
# storage saving that mattered came from ignoreCommand in vercel.json, which
# stops the ten-minute journal commits building at all; trimming the upload
# further was worth a fraction of that and cost the deployment.
journal/
site/
.venv/
design/
*.pptx
*.db
